{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, only ~3% above RNA-alone multiprofile avgpool (config_002, 0.591), and image-alone is very weak (0.208). This suggests the image modality contributes limited complementary signal and the concat fusion may be diluting the stronger RNA representation. Question: config_019 changes only the fusion method from concat to weighted, holding all other settings identical to config_018. This is a clean single-variable A/B test that isolates whether a learnable weighting can better balance the two modalities (e.g., downweighting the weak image channel). Why best next: Fusion strategy is the only design axis we have zero evidence on in the multimodal setting. The result directly determines whether future multimodal experiments should use concat or weighted fusion, and whether the image modality is genuinely adding information or acting as noise. Under a tight budget, this low-variance, high-information comparison is more valuable than jumping to a new encoder or image backbone where multiple variables would change simultaneously."
}

